This site's own change to VectorCraft, applied by build/build.sh to the release's source before debrand.py.

Objects that keep their size. An object marked data-iwdie-fixed="1" keeps its size and turn. The IWMAC Designer
Import/Export userscript marks so the IWMAC objects its Designer draws as a picture of their own size: pumps, alarms,
LEDs, valves, arrows, values' pills. A resize would only cut them off or stretch them there. With the Selection tool,
a selection of such objects has no handles and no rotate zones, so a press on it moves it. Any transform - a scale or
rotation of a selection that holds one, the Transform panel's width, the Scale and Rotate tools - moves such an object
by its centre and leaves its size and turn. A group that holds just one such object keeps its size too. This serves
the IWMAC workflow alone and is not for upstream. Keep it for every release, and carry it over by hand when it stops
fitting (UPDATING.md, When a patch stops). Tested in vectorcraft-doc (fixed_objects_keep_their_size).

